    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsDbAuditPruneTitle">Redundant Audit History Cleanup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsDbAuditPruneDesc">Transfer history details are only used to inspect which phone backed up which photos. Cleaning redundant history will never affect real photos on your PC, and the phone will still accurately skip already backed-up files next time it is connected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsDbRetentionPolicy">Retention Policy:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsBtnPruneAuditNow">Clean &amp; Optimize Now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsDbRepairTitle">Smart Self-Healing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsDbRepairDesc">If you manually deleted photos from the archive folders, leaving stale indices in the database, run one-click self-healing here: it only purges indices pointing to files that no longer exist. The system safely removes ghost records to keep the database consistent with the files, and never actively deletes any real files on your PC or phone.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsDbRepairNotice">Note: although this operation can quickly fix index issues in the database, manually deleting backed-up files is not recommended in principle — only do so when you know what you are doing. Make sure important data is backed up before proceeding.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsBtnStartRepairNow">⚡ Scan &amp; Self-Heal Now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SettingsExifToolSafetyNotice">This operation updates local file system timestamps only; it does not modify the media file's metadata or the media file itself.</sys:String>
